{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>YHWH is the righteous one, and I and my people are the wicked.</b> He says: YHWH — you who come to me by His commission, He is righteous in His judgment, in the manner of what is written (Psalms 119:137): ״צדיק אתה ה' וישר משפטיך״ — and I and my people are the wicked ones who resist His command, and who said at the outset (Exodus 1:10): ״הבה נתחכמה לו״. And because he had already denied above the unique Name, saying (Exodus 5:2): ״מי ה' אשר אשמע בקולו״, therefore he now made confession and acknowledged Him, mentioning Him in his confession both explicitly and by allusion in the initial letters. And it would have been fitting to say 'and I am the wicked one,' but he feared for his soul lest he be caught in the sin of the people, since he was king and it was in his power to protest and he did not protest; therefore he confessed on account of their sin."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:57:16.499892841Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}